WEBVTT

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:01.040
It

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:01.480
is

00:00:01.480 --> 00:00:02.080
about

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:02.780
to

00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:03.530
start!

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:19.460
Geijutsuka Art Design Class

00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:36.760
I'm heading out!

00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:50.020
Hmm? A text from Namiko-san.

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:55.280
"Sorry,

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:56.760
I'm taking the day off from school.

00:01:57.800 --> 00:02:01.030
Go on ahead. Don't wait for me at the bus stop.

00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:03.400
Also, you shouldn't read 
texts while walking..."

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:04.800
Kisa-chan! Look up! In front of you!

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:05.290
<b> Bonk</b>

00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:09.810
<b>Hexenkessel</b>

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:14.450
What? Namiko-san isn't
 coming to school today?

00:02:14.450 --> 00:02:15.430
Yes.

00:02:15.430 --> 00:02:16.620
She seems to have caught a cold.

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:18.520
Did she look sick yesterday?

00:02:17.710 --> 00:02:18.520
Here.

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:20.010
Not really.

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:20.010
Oh, thank you.

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:21.670
But she did seem a little

00:02:21.670 --> 00:02:23.720
different in her text 
she sent me yesterday.

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:25.080
Um, this one.

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:27.270
I'm getting chills,
 the edges of my eyes are burning,

00:02:27.270 --> 00:02:29.890
and I feel completely out of it.

00:02:29.890 --> 00:02:33.700
I wonder what kind of love 
sickness I caught? (LOL)

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:35.740
Namiko-san's in critical condition!

00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:38.000
She'd never normally say that!

00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:41.730
Most likely, this was because
 of painting class yesterday.

00:02:39.270 --> 00:02:45.780
<b>Sploosh</b>

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:44.100
Tomokane-dono caused 
the faucet to explode.

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:45.150
Oh, right.

00:02:46.050 --> 00:02:48.160
Man, she caught a cold from that?

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:49.050
What a wimp!

00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:50.830
She's probably asking herself

00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:52.820
why we didn't catch colds, too.

00:02:57.230 --> 00:02:57.870
Huh?

00:02:58.790 --> 00:03:00.630
Ack! If Namiko-san was here,

00:03:00.630 --> 00:03:02.260
she definitely would have
 called us out just now!

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:05.210
Are we going to make it
 through the day like this?

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:08.980
This is Namiko-san's seat.

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:10.340
It sure is lonely without her.

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:12.400
Let's do something to make things less lonely.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:13.470
Let's do something.

00:03:13.850 --> 00:03:15.510
I'll draw a bust of Namiko-san.

00:03:15.510 --> 00:03:16.450
Brilliant!

00:03:16.120 --> 00:03:31.590
<b>scribble 
scribble</b>

00:03:16.450 --> 00:03:18.880
How is Namiko-dono feeling?

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:21.680
She seems well enough to text.

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:24.720
She's responded a few times 
in the past couple of minutes.

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:27.450
They're even longer than usual.

00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:28.250
Oh.

00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:30.290
Oh! It's probably from Namiko-san.

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:31.590
Can I open it?

00:03:31.590 --> 00:03:32.100
Yes.

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:32.680
Like this?

00:03:32.680 --> 00:03:34.310
Something's still missing.

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:36.090
Kyouju-san, please read it aloud.

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:51.640
 You guys are driving 
 me cr-omanticism!

00:03:36.290 --> 00:03:38.140
I just sneezed three times 
so, if you could,

00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:41.200
go ahead and slap Noda or Tomokane.

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:39.040
Like this.

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:39.810
That's good.

00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:43.910
Kisaragi-chan! Kyouju!
 Look! Look!

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:45.710
It's like Namiko-san's here, right?

00:03:46.650 --> 00:03:49.200
What! What's with that know-it-all grin!

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:51.020
Did something happen over there just now?

00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:54.840
Huh? Kyouju-san where are you going?

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:56.920
I finished reading the book I borrowed

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:59.120
from the University Library,
 so I'm going to return it.

00:04:07.410 --> 00:04:09.590
Oh! That book looks interesting.

00:04:09.590 --> 00:04:11.620
I want to read it next,
 so let me know when you finish it.

00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:12.250
Okay.

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:22.840
Huh?

00:04:23.250 --> 00:04:26.540
The chicken lords are clustering
 around Kyouju again today.

00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:29.250
How very like Oomichi-san to read outside.

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:35.250
<b>Bzzzzzz</b>

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:35.970
Huh? Another text?
 Did I forget to turn it off?

00:04:35.970 --> 00:04:36.880
From Namiko-san?

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:40.240
It's break time right now, 
so it's okay to check your phone.

00:04:43.370 --> 00:04:44.170
Hmm?

00:04:44.170 --> 00:04:46.240
The words are all mixed up
 and I'm not sure...

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:47.130
Read it out.

00:04:47.500 --> 00:04:49.870
"Oh, I just remembered. Too bad.

00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:52.430
I'm leaving my part for you guys."

00:04:52.430 --> 00:04:53.570
She's seeing lights flash before her eyes?

00:04:53.570 --> 00:04:54.670
She's dying?

00:04:54.670 --> 00:04:57.920
Kyouju, Kisaragi-chan might
 actually take you seriously today.

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:03.460
Your still life assignments are due today

00:05:03.460 --> 00:05:05.680
so make sure you turn them in after school.

00:05:05.930 --> 00:05:07.220
That's right.

00:05:07.220 --> 00:05:09.020
Didn't she say last week 
that they were due today?

00:05:09.020 --> 00:05:10.870
Oh, so that text just now...

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:12.420
Was about the assignment.

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:14.430
I get it!

00:05:14.430 --> 00:05:15.890
Leave it to us, Namiko-san.

00:05:15.890 --> 00:05:18.180
We accept that responsibility!

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:18.560
<b> Bzzzzz</b>

00:05:18.690 --> 00:05:19.510
All right!

00:05:19.510 --> 00:05:21.990
I'll finish up the right side, so Noda take the left.

00:05:21.150 --> 00:05:22.330
<b> Bang</b>

00:05:21.990 --> 00:05:24.170
Let's paint with our get-well wishes a

00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:23.570
<b>Sploosh</b>

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:24.840
 Hee-yah!

00:05:24.170 --> 00:05:25.580
fauvist painting of overflowing passion!

00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:26.070
<b> Hurrrr!</b>

00:05:25.950 --> 00:05:30.040
"I took some medicine,
 but these chills just won't go away."

00:05:26.140 --> 00:05:27.340
<b>Go Go!</b>

00:05:27.370 --> 00:05:28.570
<b> Ahhhhhh!</b>

00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:30.680
<b> Bam! Pow!</b>

00:05:32.910 --> 00:05:35.330
How has Namiko-san been since then?

00:05:35.330 --> 00:05:36.580
Oh, about that:

00:05:36.580 --> 00:05:38.950
I haven't got a single text since then.

00:05:38.950 --> 00:05:39.620
I see.

00:05:39.620 --> 00:05:41.220
She might be sleeping right now.

00:05:41.420 --> 00:05:45.230
Just in case, I've been
 texting her during the breaks.

00:05:45.230 --> 00:05:48.440
Thinking maybe she's getting lonely missing school.

00:05:48.440 --> 00:05:50.230
Hmm. Is that how it works?

00:05:50.900 --> 00:05:53.600
My brother spends half his life in bed and

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:55.590
he isn't lonely at all, if anything...

00:05:55.590 --> 00:05:57.750
There seems to be someone who looks like a

00:05:57.750 --> 00:05:59.500
bleached version of Tomokane-san right behind-

00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:00.200
Ack!

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:01.740
Oh!

00:06:01.740 --> 00:06:03.510
Nurse's Office

00:06:05.430 --> 00:06:06.360
Oh, are you feeling better?

00:06:06.700 --> 00:06:09.590
Yes, but when did I get here?

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:13.090
Apparently, you didn't feel well during lunch.

00:06:13.090 --> 00:06:14.650
A short-haired girl who looks like you

00:06:14.650 --> 00:06:16.550
with a lot of energy brought you

00:06:16.550 --> 00:06:19.160
and threw you inside before leaving.

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:22.660
I see. Sorry for all the excitement.

00:06:24.810 --> 00:06:27.180
We're already in our afternoon classes.

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:29.930
I wonder if Namiko-san is feeling any better.

00:06:30.440 --> 00:06:32.740
Is she up watching TV?

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:34.940
Or sleeping in her room?

00:06:36.370 --> 00:06:38.600
Why do I feel so uneasy

00:06:38.600 --> 00:06:40.900
when I don't feel her presence or see her face?

00:06:42.950 --> 00:06:44.450
Three more minutes.

00:06:44.610 --> 00:06:46.600
Somehow... Yamaguchi-san's expression

00:06:46.600 --> 00:06:47.950
is a little different today, isn't it?

00:06:47.950 --> 00:06:50.490
This hint of exhaustion... of sorrow...

00:06:50.490 --> 00:06:52.540
inspires my desire to create!

00:06:53.650 --> 00:06:55.730
Lots of things happened today!

00:06:58.330 --> 00:06:59.690
Kisaragi-chan, what should we do?

00:07:00.190 --> 00:07:02.000
Should we go? Or not?

00:07:02.170 --> 00:07:02.900
Remember?

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:04.720
The famous cake shop in our area that I was

00:07:04.720 --> 00:07:06.000
talking about last week.

00:07:06.150 --> 00:07:07.870
Today's their all-you-can-eat buffet day

00:07:07.870 --> 00:07:09.730
and we were saying we would
 all go together, remember?

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:12.530
It's called the Western Sweets Workshop.

00:07:13.020 --> 00:07:13.870
Oh.

00:07:14.840 --> 00:07:17.170
No. Today is a little...

00:07:17.170 --> 00:07:18.700
Mmm, okay.

00:07:18.700 --> 00:07:21.450
Tomokane and Kyouju feel the same way, so...

00:07:21.850 --> 00:07:23.610
Then, I'll see you tomorrow!

00:07:27.620 --> 00:07:31.400
I see. That text was about the cake shop.

00:07:31.250 --> 00:07:33.230
<b> Bzzzzzz</b>

00:07:37.360 --> 00:07:39.490
"I guess I fell asleep without noticing.

00:07:39.490 --> 00:07:41.510
Have you stuffed yourself with cake yet?

00:07:41.670 --> 00:07:44.920
Also, sorry for texting you so much today.

00:07:47.090 --> 00:07:48.620
When I catch colds,

00:07:48.620 --> 00:07:50.700
I get oddly lonely,

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:52.750
so I really appreciated it.
 (LOL)"

00:07:56.950 --> 00:08:00.760
The next morning, 
Namiko-san came to school as usual.

00:08:01.130 --> 00:08:02.260
Good morning.

00:08:02.460 --> 00:08:04.160
Are you feeling better?

00:08:04.160 --> 00:08:07.530
Yup. Well, my body still feels a little achy,

00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:10.700
but I really just wanted to talk to everyone so.

00:08:10.700 --> 00:08:13.540
I couldn't sit around sleeping all
 day again, so I came to school.

00:08:13.780 --> 00:08:15.620
No, really. I'm fine.

00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:17.540
I don't have a fever anymore.

00:08:17.910 --> 00:08:21.320
Oh, but I did miss out on the cake buffet.

00:08:21.320 --> 00:08:24.050
Let's all go together sometime.

00:08:24.050 --> 00:08:25.420
Oh, yeah.

00:08:25.420 --> 00:08:26.830
Yesterday I bought some crème brûlée

00:08:26.830 --> 00:08:28.640
from the Western Sweets workshop instead,

00:08:28.640 --> 00:08:29.920
so let's eat it at lunch.

00:08:29.920 --> 00:08:32.180
Ooh, and I'll have to work quickly today

00:08:30.340 --> 00:08:31.720
Oh, what's it like? Let me see.

00:08:31.720 --> 00:08:32.800
Just to see.

00:08:32.180 --> 00:08:34.030
and finish up the still life assignment.

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:34.930
Whaat?!

00:08:36.900 --> 00:08:38.930
Hey, Namiko-san.

00:08:38.930 --> 00:08:42.900
Are you sure you're not 
feeling even the tiniest bit sick?

00:08:42.910 --> 00:08:44.140
Just to be safe,

00:08:44.140 --> 00:08:47.320
don't you feel like maybe taking
 an hour in the nurse's office?

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:48.760
I'm feeling like someone might

00:08:48.760 --> 00:08:51.240
need to visit the nurse's office soon. 
Parenthesis LOL.

00:08:53.030 --> 00:08:55.230
You look worse than I do.

00:08:55.230 --> 00:08:56.590
Oh, really?

00:08:56.580 --> 00:08:59.050
Geijutsuka Art Design Class

00:08:59.050 --> 00:09:03.050
Hot pot, hot pot, hot pot...

00:09:03.740 --> 00:09:06.760
In this way, the color, light and
 darkness, and use of brushstrokes

00:09:06.760 --> 00:09:09.640
in the background of a painting, 
act to express the heart

00:09:09.640 --> 00:09:12.560
of the painter or, in other 
words, the creator's sentiment.

00:09:12.560 --> 00:09:15.710
This month we'll be looking 
at the “expression of feeling”

00:09:15.710 --> 00:09:18.180
and this will be the theme of
 the assignment you will submit.

00:09:19.560 --> 00:09:22.700
Something along the lines 
of happiness or rage is fine.

00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:25.070
I'll leave an example so please take a look.

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:27.950
Submit a piece of B4 size or larger.

00:09:28.480 --> 00:09:31.650
If I place it behind like this,
 maybe it's easier to understand?

00:09:31.650 --> 00:09:35.220
See? Doesn't it seem like I'm a little depressed?

00:09:35.240 --> 00:09:42.710
<b> Sob sob</b>

00:09:35.640 --> 00:09:37.530
By the way, this is how

00:09:37.530 --> 00:09:40.030
I felt about the submissions 
from the last assignment.

00:09:40.190 --> 00:09:42.730
I wonder if the teacher 
made those on purpose.

00:09:43.080 --> 00:09:46.000
This time we got another difficult assignment.

00:09:46.130 --> 00:09:49.700
I wish they'd put a little more
 fun into these assignments, right?

00:09:49.700 --> 00:09:51.090
Like me!

00:09:51.090 --> 00:09:54.410
Noda, you always submit 
your assignments so early, huh?

00:09:54.420 --> 00:09:58.410
 Sotoma-sensei in the Staff Room

00:10:01.640 --> 00:10:02.810
Is Noda here?

00:10:03.170 --> 00:10:04.730
She quickly packed and left.

00:10:04.730 --> 00:10:05.790
I see!

00:10:06.620 --> 00:10:09.350
But this week we have exhibition work too,

00:10:09.350 --> 00:10:11.270
so I'd like to submit this early.

00:10:11.270 --> 00:10:12.550
Then, want to do it together?

00:10:12.550 --> 00:10:13.720
It'd be more efficient right?

00:10:14.610 --> 00:10:17.000
But we can't use the art room today, so...

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:17.870
No, at my house.

00:10:17.870 --> 00:10:21.150
Namiko-dono and I were just
 talking about finishing our

00:10:21.150 --> 00:10:23.320
exhibition work while we're off today and tomorrow.

00:10:24.810 --> 00:10:26.400
Like a sleepover?

00:10:26.400 --> 00:10:28.570
If you don't mind going straight there.

00:10:28.570 --> 00:10:30.090
My house is a fair ways away

00:10:30.090 --> 00:10:32.480
from the suburbs, so it's pretty far.

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:33.720
It's a long walk.

00:10:33.770 --> 00:10:35.490
It'd be dangerous to go just with girls

00:10:35.490 --> 00:10:36.900
to a place like that!
 I'll come too!

00:10:36.900 --> 00:10:37.660
How rude.

00:10:37.660 --> 00:10:40.020
Couldn't you just have
honestly said you wanted to come?

00:10:40.150 --> 00:10:41.290
I want to go!

00:10:41.440 --> 00:10:43.050
So can I call Noda, too?

00:10:43.050 --> 00:10:43.900
Sure.

00:10:44.300 --> 00:10:46.670
I should probably let her know 
that more people are coming.

00:10:46.670 --> 00:10:47.600
Your mother?

00:10:47.930 --> 00:10:48.800
Oh, Noda?

00:10:48.800 --> 00:10:49.430
You busy?

00:10:49.680 --> 00:10:52.770
Kisaragi was saying that she 
wanted to finish her assignment,

00:10:52.770 --> 00:10:55.880
so so Namiko-san said that Kyouju
and her were going to stay over and...

00:10:55.880 --> 00:10:58.380
Tomokane-san could you 
maybe get to the point?

00:10:58.380 --> 00:11:00.590
Wanna go assault Namiko-san's house?

00:11:00.590 --> 00:11:01.710
That's the point?!

00:11:02.650 --> 00:11:03.710
And Noda-dono?

00:11:03.710 --> 00:11:05.210
She said okay twice.

00:11:05.500 --> 00:11:06.970
Is this really okay?

00:11:06.970 --> 00:11:10.210
I mean suddenly dropping
 in with so many people.

00:11:10.210 --> 00:11:11.520
Oh, it's fine.

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:13.260
She said she doesn't know what everyone likes

00:11:13.260 --> 00:11:15.500
so just buy dinner on your way over.

00:11:15.500 --> 00:11:17.190
What should we do?
 What do you want?

00:11:17.190 --> 00:11:19.570
Since we're eating together,
 then maybe a hot pot or something.

00:11:19.570 --> 00:11:20.520
We already have rice.

00:11:20.520 --> 00:11:21.960
I'll ask Noda.

00:11:22.260 --> 00:11:23.550
Hmm? Dinner?

00:11:23.550 --> 00:11:26.100
Oh! I want to eat <i>that thing</i>.

00:11:26.100 --> 00:11:27.120
Yami-nabe?

00:11:26.100 --> 00:11:27.120
 Yami-nabe = Darkness hot pot

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:27.780
Yami-nabe?

00:11:27.780 --> 00:11:28.730
Yami-nabe?

00:11:31.370 --> 00:11:33.160
She sure keeps us waiting.

00:11:33.160 --> 00:11:34.160
Sorry for the wait!

00:11:34.160 --> 00:11:35.500
Noda, you're late!

00:11:35.500 --> 00:11:36.740
You already went home?

00:11:36.760 --> 00:11:38.730
 Late Nights   Open 'til 1am

00:11:39.060 --> 00:11:41.150
Are we really doing yami-nabe?

00:11:40.030 --> 00:11:41.150
<b>Ooh!</b>

00:11:41.380 --> 00:11:44.210
Well, the majority wanted it.

00:11:44.210 --> 00:11:47.620
I didn't think that Masa would 
agree, but what can you do.

00:11:47.620 --> 00:11:48.790
Let's get hot pot ingredients.

00:11:49.410 --> 00:11:50.740
Okay, insert basket.

00:11:50.740 --> 00:11:51.640
Basket!

00:11:51.640 --> 00:11:52.630
Okay, insert Noda.

00:11:52.630 --> 00:11:53.240
Noda!

00:11:53.240 --> 00:11:54.200
I won't fit!

00:11:55.930 --> 00:11:58.600
Is it okay if we just get 
normal hot pot ingredients?

00:11:58.600 --> 00:12:00.030
Well, it is a hot pot.

00:12:00.030 --> 00:12:01.780
Since it's a yami-nabe

00:12:01.780 --> 00:12:04.340
I thought maybe we needed
 something more eccentric.

00:12:04.340 --> 00:12:06.070
Well, we're the ones eating it,

00:12:06.070 --> 00:12:07.310
so it's probably good not to go overboard.

00:12:07.310 --> 00:12:08.810
Namiko-san, Namiko-san!

00:12:08.810 --> 00:12:10.010
Where are the scrubbing brushes?

00:12:10.010 --> 00:12:12.470
Where do they sell socks and rubber boots?

00:12:12.470 --> 00:12:14.100
Be reasonable!

00:12:12.590 --> 00:12:14.810
<b>Everyday Goods are on the 2nd Floor</b>

00:12:14.100 --> 00:12:14.810
Darn.

00:12:20.360 --> 00:12:21.410
We're here.

00:12:21.410 --> 00:12:23.150
Phew. We walked a lot.

00:12:23.600 --> 00:12:24.220
I'm home!

00:12:24.220 --> 00:12:25.770
Come on in.

00:12:24.220 --> 00:12:25.770
There's a dog!

00:12:25.770 --> 00:12:26.710
Welcome!

00:12:26.710 --> 00:12:28.520
My! There sure are a lot of you!

00:12:28.520 --> 00:12:29.380
Nice to meet you.

00:12:29.380 --> 00:12:30.330
Sorry to intrude.

00:12:30.330 --> 00:12:31.270
Come on in!

00:12:31.270 --> 00:12:32.170
Later, dog.

00:12:31.610 --> 00:12:34.430
You must be Kisaragi-chan and Masa-chan.

00:12:35.410 --> 00:12:37.800
I'm sorry our Namiko is always giving you trouble.

00:12:37.800 --> 00:12:39.980
We're always worried that our friend is

00:12:39.980 --> 00:12:41.840
giving you a headache while she's away.

00:12:41.840 --> 00:12:45.140
You all are just like she said.

00:12:45.560 --> 00:12:51.480
<b> Bang bang</b>

00:12:45.860 --> 00:12:48.040
Is it all right to leave our stuff here?

00:12:48.040 --> 00:12:48.650
Sure.

00:12:48.650 --> 00:12:50.510
Namiko-san, what about tea for the guests?

00:12:50.510 --> 00:12:51.480
Just go home already.

00:12:51.480 --> 00:12:52.110
No.

00:12:52.110 --> 00:12:54.560
Oh, by the way, is this room
too cramped to sleep in?

00:12:54.560 --> 00:12:56.110
It's fine. We can sleep like sardines.

00:12:56.110 --> 00:12:57.800
Oh! What character should we make?

00:12:57.800 --> 00:12:59.010
We can go up to five strokes!

00:12:59.010 --> 00:12:59.920
Don't worry.

00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:02.560
I definitely won't let anybody sleep!

00:13:02.580 --> 00:13:03.190
Leave it to me!

00:13:03.950 --> 00:13:05.520
I guess Noda will fit in here.

00:13:05.520 --> 00:13:06.460
Isolation?!

00:13:08.470 --> 00:13:09.660
Let's hot pot!

00:13:09.660 --> 00:13:10.930
Let's hot pot!

00:13:10.930 --> 00:13:12.770
First, we had Namiko-san

00:13:12.770 --> 00:13:14.250
and Kisaragi-chan, by ladder lottery,

00:13:14.250 --> 00:13:15.940
choose the soup flavor
 and the seasonings!

00:13:15.760 --> 00:13:16.310
<b>Ooh!</b>

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:18.640
And the results:
 Oh! They go well together.

00:13:18.640 --> 00:13:19.940
The seasoning is Kimchi.

00:13:19.940 --> 00:13:21.030
Oh, that's pretty normal.

00:13:21.030 --> 00:13:22.290
The flavor is ramune candies.

00:13:22.290 --> 00:13:23.200
How are they similar?

00:13:23.200 --> 00:13:24.450
The only thing they 
have in common is “mu”.

00:13:24.730 --> 00:13:26.720
Hmm. Might work.

00:13:28.370 --> 00:13:29.360
Let's hot pot!

00:13:29.360 --> 00:13:30.600
Let's hot pot!

00:13:30.600 --> 00:13:33.360
Take out anything that needs to be cut or washed.

00:13:33.360 --> 00:13:33.860
Yes!

00:13:34.150 --> 00:13:36.640
Oh, this bag is all sweets.

00:13:36.640 --> 00:13:38.370
She got a lot.

00:13:38.370 --> 00:13:40.630
Is she planning on eating snacks 
on top of having a hot pot?

00:13:40.630 --> 00:13:42.910
Nope, those are for the hot pot as well.

00:13:43.570 --> 00:13:44.640
Right?

00:13:44.640 --> 00:13:45.990
What?!

00:13:49.870 --> 00:13:52.170
A yami-nabe is where everyone chooses

00:13:52.170 --> 00:13:53.770
a secret ingredient and then,

00:13:53.770 --> 00:13:56.460
with the lights off,
 adds that ingredient to the pot.

00:13:56.460 --> 00:13:59.260
While it boils and until you choose
 something with your chopsticks

00:13:59.260 --> 00:14:00.780
the lights remain off, 
or so they say.

00:14:00.820 --> 00:14:02.290
That's an interesting face.

00:14:02.290 --> 00:14:05.030
Since we already know
 all of the ingredients

00:14:02.300 --> 00:14:28.210
 Bubble

00:14:05.030 --> 00:14:09.140
let's do a yami-nabe from
 when we take off the lid.

00:14:09.140 --> 00:14:12.930
There's a thrill in not
 knowing what's in the pot.

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:15.460
But I believe this is the only opportunity

00:14:15.460 --> 00:14:17.530
I will have to experience a yami-nabe.

00:14:17.530 --> 00:14:19.940
Oh! How unusually enthusiastic of you, Kyouju!

00:14:19.940 --> 00:14:21.010
Wearing such a happy face!

00:14:21.010 --> 00:14:21.970
Me too! Me too!

00:14:21.970 --> 00:14:23.500
I'm so excited!

00:14:23.860 --> 00:14:25.550
In terms of our assignment,
 it'd be like this, right?

00:14:25.550 --> 00:14:27.010
You finished already?!

00:14:27.010 --> 00:14:28.210
You really are enthusiastic.

00:14:28.450 --> 00:14:29.980
The ingredients are cut.

00:14:29.980 --> 00:14:32.720
We had Namiko-san's 
mother cut them for us.

00:14:32.860 --> 00:14:35.130
The ramune candy broth is ready, too.

00:14:35.130 --> 00:14:37.150
At a glance it looks like regular boiling water...

00:14:37.150 --> 00:14:37.970
Want a taste?

00:14:37.970 --> 00:14:38.720
I'll pass.

00:14:38.720 --> 00:14:40.100
Then I'll put them in.

00:14:40.100 --> 00:14:41.980
Chinese cabbage, tofu...

00:14:41.980 --> 00:14:43.200
Oh, steaming up!

00:14:43.200 --> 00:14:44.760
We should leave the meat for later, right?

00:14:44.760 --> 00:14:45.720
Candy drops!

00:14:45.720 --> 00:14:46.760
Potato chips!

00:14:46.760 --> 00:14:47.730
Canned peach!

00:14:47.730 --> 00:14:48.500
Chocolate puffs!

00:14:48.500 --> 00:14:50.550
You better eat this! You most certainly are going to eat this!

00:14:48.900 --> 00:14:51.510
We can leave the sweet potato jelly and melon bread for later, right?

00:14:50.550 --> 00:14:52.000
Namiko-san! Calm down!

00:14:52.250 --> 00:14:54.370
Okay, so we've added everything we have to add.

00:14:54.370 --> 00:14:56.510
I guess we just have to wait until it's done.

00:14:56.810 --> 00:14:59.240
You have to wait until the last second to open the lid.

00:14:59.240 --> 00:15:00.690
So you don't see what's inside.

00:15:00.690 --> 00:15:01.570
Right, right.

00:15:01.570 --> 00:15:04.320
To take it this far is very exciting!

00:15:04.320 --> 00:15:07.290
We haven't forgotten to do anything, right?

00:15:07.290 --> 00:15:09.450
No. All that's left is...

00:15:11.560 --> 00:15:12.600
To write our wills.

00:15:12.600 --> 00:15:13.240
Of course!

00:15:13.240 --> 00:15:14.030
Oh no!

00:15:14.340 --> 00:15:17.210
It might be good to take out some of the lye.

00:15:17.210 --> 00:15:18.030
Yeah!

00:15:18.240 --> 00:15:19.820
I'm opening it.

00:15:25.790 --> 00:15:27.720
Well, um...

00:15:28.160 --> 00:15:31.830
It was so chaotic in there, I wasn't sure what was lye.

00:15:32.040 --> 00:15:34.160
This is no longer a yami-nabe.

00:15:34.160 --> 00:15:35.960
Perhaps we should call it chaos-nabe.

00:15:35.960 --> 00:15:37.170
It surpasses darkness?

00:15:37.170 --> 00:15:38.640
Should I add some spice?

00:15:38.640 --> 00:15:39.540
For our stomachs.

00:15:39.540 --> 00:15:41.480
What's with the old man's gag?

00:15:44.440 --> 00:15:47.110
Now, before we eat, 
we mustn't forget

00:15:47.110 --> 00:15:49.060
our other objective: the assignment.

00:15:49.360 --> 00:15:52.460
Have you recorded your
 current emotions in your sketchbooks?

00:15:52.460 --> 00:15:53.500
Yes!

00:15:53.500 --> 00:15:54.650
Ready and...

00:15:54.650 --> 00:15:55.670
Reveal!

00:15:57.310 --> 00:15:59.650
The person who seems most excited right now is...

00:16:01.360 --> 00:16:02.370
Kyouju?

00:16:03.050 --> 00:16:04.540
Okay. I'm opening it.

00:16:07.260 --> 00:16:10.210
 Bubble, bubble...

00:16:10.910 --> 00:16:13.140
Is this what a witch's hot pot looks like?

00:16:13.140 --> 00:16:16.070
It sure has a strange smell... 
kind of sweet.

00:16:16.070 --> 00:16:19.590
In a manga, it might 
shoot bubbles or spit fire at us.

00:16:19.590 --> 00:16:20.860
I tried copying it.

00:16:20.860 --> 00:16:22.290
That's amazing, Kyouju!

00:16:23.330 --> 00:16:25.680
If you put Kisaragi-chan in front,
 it looks like this.

00:16:26.030 --> 00:16:28.870
It's as if she can see 
what's about to happen to us.

00:16:29.030 --> 00:16:30.860
All right Namiko-san,
 turn off the lights.

00:16:30.860 --> 00:16:31.640
Okay. Okay.

00:16:31.930 --> 00:16:33.640
Whoa! It's darker than
 I thought it would be.

00:16:34.270 --> 00:16:36.610
Now the feast begins!

00:16:38.250 --> 00:16:40.280
What? What are you drawing?

00:16:40.560 --> 00:16:42.650
<b>Cackle cackle</b>

00:16:42.850 --> 00:16:44.410
Did everyone take an ingredient?

00:16:44.410 --> 00:16:45.920
Turn the lights on!

00:16:46.060 --> 00:16:47.570
Wha! What is this?

00:16:47.570 --> 00:16:49.960
A peach?
 A kimchi flavored peach?

00:16:47.940 --> 00:16:53.420
<b> Snip snip</b>

00:16:49.960 --> 00:16:51.610
What could mine be?

00:16:51.610 --> 00:16:53.420
It looks like it's oozing.

00:16:53.420 --> 00:16:55.150
I got meat.

00:16:55.450 --> 00:16:56.850
Kyouju, what did you get?

00:16:56.850 --> 00:16:57.570
Tofu.

00:16:57.570 --> 00:16:58.570
How normal!

00:16:58.570 --> 00:17:01.060
I found candy drops and 
chocolate puffs inside, though.

00:17:01.060 --> 00:17:02.810
What a deceptive trick!

00:17:02.950 --> 00:17:03.700
 Hfft

00:17:12.690 --> 00:17:14.360
All right, Kisaragi-chan! Taste it!

00:17:13.730 --> 00:17:14.480
<b>Heh heh heh</b>

00:17:14.360 --> 00:17:15.430
Me?

00:17:15.430 --> 00:17:17.720
We're counting on your gourmet
 cuisine commentary, Kisaragi!

00:17:21.240 --> 00:17:21.490
<b> Chomp</b>

00:17:21.810 --> 00:17:23.090
What is Kisaragi's?

00:17:23.090 --> 00:17:24.840
Um, I think it's probably melon bread.

00:17:24.840 --> 00:17:27.060
Oh, it was all drippy and oozy because

00:17:27.060 --> 00:17:28.730
it sucked up all the chaos liquid.

00:17:28.730 --> 00:17:29.730
Kisaragi?

00:17:30.810 --> 00:17:33.230
This is where we show off 
our skills as developing artists!

00:17:33.230 --> 00:17:36.160
Based on her expression, 
determine her inner feelings!

00:17:38.120 --> 00:17:39.040
Too delicious!

00:17:39.040 --> 00:17:39.840
Seriously?

00:17:41.030 --> 00:17:41.820
Hell!

00:17:42.290 --> 00:17:43.300
And heaven!

00:17:43.300 --> 00:17:44.340
What?!

00:17:47.220 --> 00:17:51.060
Its taste far surpassed what 
I had expected or prepared for.

00:17:51.520 --> 00:17:52.650
This is definitely...

00:17:52.650 --> 00:17:55.210
Kyouju-san, you're eating very calmly.

00:17:55.210 --> 00:17:56.240
Masa, is it good?

00:17:56.240 --> 00:17:56.820
Not at all.

00:17:56.820 --> 00:17:58.360
I see. That's a relief.

00:17:58.510 --> 00:18:00.170
I thought Noda and Tomokane were a little quiet,

00:18:00.170 --> 00:18:01.910
but it looks like they're just busy eating.

00:18:01.960 --> 00:18:05.320
Since it was their idea,
 they can't really complain.

00:18:05.320 --> 00:18:06.300
Wait that's a drawing, isn't it?!

00:18:06.810 --> 00:18:09.120
Somehow we hadn't put in any sandals!

00:18:10.280 --> 00:18:13.920
Hm. There still appears 
to be plenty of hot pot.

00:18:13.920 --> 00:18:15.800
We can't afford to keep nibbling.

00:18:15.800 --> 00:18:17.140
We'll have to divide this up.

00:18:20.580 --> 00:18:23.210
You gave us way more!

00:18:23.210 --> 00:18:24.180
What is this?!

00:18:24.180 --> 00:18:25.680
Obviously it's a responsibility tax!

00:18:25.680 --> 00:18:26.520
Tax?!

00:18:26.520 --> 00:18:29.060
There still looks like there's enough for seconds.

00:18:42.560 --> 00:18:45.330
I can't eat anymore.

00:18:45.330 --> 00:18:46.470
Are you okay?

00:18:46.470 --> 00:18:48.300
Hey, witch girl.

00:18:48.300 --> 00:18:50.770
I'm begging you.
 Erase this hot pot with magic.

00:18:50.770 --> 00:18:52.140
Oh, I can't.

00:18:52.140 --> 00:18:55.360
If I use magic, then I get
 kicked out of the human world.

00:18:55.710 --> 00:18:56.450
What's that?

00:18:56.850 --> 00:18:59.420
What are you studying magic for
 if you can't even practice it?

00:18:59.740 --> 00:19:02.460
It sure is pretty mushy.

00:19:07.660 --> 00:19:08.910
Oh, it's not a picture.

00:19:09.230 --> 00:19:11.030
Kisaragi, wake up!

00:19:13.150 --> 00:19:16.000
It's finally done...

00:19:19.250 --> 00:19:22.670
Mastermind Noda, do you have anything to add?

00:19:22.670 --> 00:19:25.970
A-always think your evil plans through.

00:19:32.310 --> 00:19:34.220
So that's what you did over the weekend!

00:19:34.220 --> 00:19:36.770
Yes... and thanks to it, 
my stomach still feels like lead.

00:19:36.770 --> 00:19:39.180
I guess you have friends like that, too.

00:19:39.180 --> 00:19:41.780
It's fun hearing about it, but...

00:19:41.780 --> 00:19:43.560
When you really do it, 
it sure is troublesome.

00:19:43.770 --> 00:19:45.830
You didn't buy any curry roux?

00:19:45.830 --> 00:19:47.570
Curry? No, why?

00:19:48.130 --> 00:19:50.190
Because if you add curry at the end,

00:19:50.190 --> 00:19:52.430
just about anything becomes bearable, right?

00:19:53.080 --> 00:19:56.010
“Right?” Sounds like you've
 had some experience with this.

00:19:56.010 --> 00:19:57.340
Buchi-san!

00:19:56.720 --> 00:19:57.340
My, my.

00:19:57.340 --> 00:19:58.610
Let's hot pot!

00:19:58.610 --> 00:19:59.940
Details in the art room!

00:19:59.940 --> 00:20:01.410
See you later!

00:20:02.190 --> 00:20:03.790
Your president, right?

00:20:03.790 --> 00:20:05.200
Who's a yami-nabe fan.

00:20:05.200 --> 00:20:06.620
I see.

00:20:10.160 --> 00:20:13.890
So many submissions right after the weekend!

00:20:13.890 --> 00:20:15.600
Thank you! Thank you!

00:20:15.600 --> 00:20:17.700
Professor, it's not right to thank us.

00:20:17.700 --> 00:20:20.510
Huh? Is this piece by 
Oomichi-san supposed to be

00:20:20.510 --> 00:20:21.900
a metaphor for something?

00:20:22.040 --> 00:20:22.730
Yes.

00:20:22.730 --> 00:20:24.800
Ooh, Kyouju, this is exactly how it was!

00:20:24.820 --> 00:20:31.810
GA-1 Oomichi Miyabi
<Title> Witch's Cauldron

00:20:25.460 --> 00:20:30.080
An idiom from foreign countries
meaning “chaotic” or “confusing”.

00:20:31.830 --> 00:20:33.800
<b> Fine Arts Club In Session</b>

00:20:33.890 --> 00:20:35.210
I had totally forgotten about it,

00:20:35.210 --> 00:20:37.920
but we haven't done a welcoming 
party for our new member!

00:20:37.920 --> 00:20:40.320
So this year let's do that! 
Let's do that!

00:20:40.410 --> 00:20:42.180
So we really are doing that, after all.

00:20:42.180 --> 00:20:43.430
I'm fine with a welcoming party,

00:20:43.430 --> 00:20:44.840
but do we have to do that?

00:20:44.840 --> 00:20:46.250
What do you mean by that?

00:20:46.250 --> 00:20:47.180
Yami-nabe.

00:20:47.180 --> 00:20:48.960
Ohh, that sounds fun!

00:20:48.960 --> 00:20:49.690
Right?

00:20:49.930 --> 00:20:52.050
If you get carried away 
and put in inedible things,

00:20:52.050 --> 00:20:53.620
Tomokane will break.

00:20:53.620 --> 00:20:55.560
Ahh, so that's fair game as well, is it?

00:20:55.560 --> 00:20:58.570
I got a stomachache last year,
 but only took a day off.

00:20:58.810 --> 00:21:01.630
All right, then as a special rule this time,

00:21:01.630 --> 00:21:03.300
all ingredients will be edible.

00:21:03.300 --> 00:21:05.200
Theme: Healthy Yami-Nabe!

00:21:04.350 --> 00:21:05.200
Oh! Sounds good.

00:21:05.200 --> 00:21:06.440
Oh, Professor.

00:21:06.440 --> 00:21:08.550
There was some limestone
 in the preparation room, right?

00:21:08.550 --> 00:21:09.510
Huh? Limestone?

00:21:09.510 --> 00:21:10.140
Why?

00:21:10.140 --> 00:21:10.950
Calcium.

00:21:11.170 --> 00:21:13.860
I'll go around the school and 
look for medicinal plants!

00:21:13.860 --> 00:21:15.220
Leave the mushrooms.

00:21:15.220 --> 00:21:17.260
I wonder what I should choose.

00:21:17.950 --> 00:21:20.730
What club is this supposed to be again?

00:21:25.740 --> 00:21:26.770
Look, look!

00:21:25.750 --> 00:21:28.500
 Baked Sweets 
 Half Price 
 Japanese Autumn Appreciation Festical, Today only

00:21:26.770 --> 00:21:28.500
Today, baked sweets are half price!

00:21:28.500 --> 00:21:29.270
What do you think?

00:21:29.270 --> 00:21:33.400
Mm, today I was thinking of 
working on my exhibition assignment.

00:21:33.400 --> 00:21:35.470
Me, too. I'm being unusually studious.

00:21:35.470 --> 00:21:36.680
Masa, what about you?

00:21:36.680 --> 00:21:38.480
As long as I'm with everyone else...

00:21:38.480 --> 00:21:40.110
Kisaragi, it's half price today!

00:21:40.110 --> 00:21:41.250
Let's work on the assignment tomorrow!

00:21:41.250 --> 00:21:42.010
That sounds good!

00:21:42.320 --> 00:21:43.240
Then,

00:21:43.240 --> 00:21:44.520
let's all go together!

00:21:44.520 --> 00:21:45.590
Yay!

00:21:48.020 --> 00:21:48.920
Let's go to karaoke too.

00:21:48.920 --> 00:21:50.600
Oh! I have some discount coupons!

00:21:50.570 --> 00:21:53.450
Some people sure do use a cute voice when they sing.

00:21:51.080 --> 00:21:53.270
Kyouju-san what sort of songs do you sing?

00:21:53.450 --> 00:21:54.330
Oh, like Namiko-san, right?

00:21:54.330 --> 00:21:55.030
You mean Tomokane.
